@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cpi-il35-nouns`
IMPORT `cpi-il35-published-figures`

-- Row IL-35: "the index" and "the rate of rise of the index" as the Income Tax Ordinance s 1 and the National
-- Insurance Law s 1 word them, over the Bureau's published readings (cpi-il35-published-figures.l4: DATA, NOT LAW).
-- Quotations (`src:N`) are copied mechanically from line N of
--   ../../../income-tax-ordinance-new-version/registers/source-bundle/income-tax-ordinance-new-version.he.wiki.txt  (ITO)
--   ../../registers/source-bundle/national-insurance-law-consolidated-version-5755-1995.he.wiki.txt                  (NII)
-- by tools/srcquote.py. Every `-- src:N |` line here is from the Ordinance (ITO s 1); the National Insurance Law's
-- s 1 "מדד" (NII line 171) is quoted in nii-s334-index.l4.
--
-- WHAT THE LAWS SAY. Both name the index the Bureau publishes (ITO: "מדד המחירים לצרכן שמפרסמת הלשכה המרכזית
-- לסטטיסטיקה"; NII: the same, "published monthly", NII line 171), and the ITO defines the rate of rise "in a period" by two readings:
-- the one published last before the END of the period and the one published last before its START, the difference
-- divided by the latter. Neither says anything of rounding. Neither has an "index for a year": a year's rise is the
-- rise over the period of the year.
--
-- WHICH READING IS "PUBLISHED LAST BEFORE". A month's reading is published in the next month (assumption A1,
-- cpi-il35-published-figures.l4). So the reading published last before the START of month M (before M's first day) is
-- the reading of month M-2, and the one published last before the END of month M (before M's last day) is the reading
-- of month M-1. For a tax year, which begins 1 January, the first is November of the year before and the second is
-- November of the same year.

§ `The month arithmetic the readings need`

GIVEN `the month` IS A `A calendar month`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the running number of` `the month` MEANS
    (`the month`'s `year of the month` TIMES 12) PLUS (`the month`'s `number of the month in the year`) MINUS 1

GIVEN `the running number` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A calendar month`
`the calendar month with running number` `the running number` MEANS
    `A calendar month`
        WITH `year of the month`               IS (`the running number` MINUS (`the running number` MODULO 12)) DIVIDED BY 12
        ,    `number of the month in the year` IS (`the running number` MODULO 12) PLUS 1

GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of the month` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A calendar month`
`the calendar month in year` `the year` `, number` `the number of the month` MEANS
    `A calendar month` WITH `year of the month` IS `the year`, `number of the month in the year` IS `the number of the month`

§ `Reading the published series`

@ref cpi-il35-published-figures.l4: the series begins with January 2000
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the published series begins with January 2000, so the reading this needs is not in it` MEANS
    REFUSE "the published series begins with January 2000, so the reading this needs is not in it"

@ref cpi-il35-published-figures.l4: the series ends with August 2026
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the published series ends with August 2026, so the reading this needs is not in it` MEANS
    REFUSE "the published series ends with August 2026 (the sources deposited); the reading this needs is later and is not in it"

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the series has no reading for a month between its first and last` MEANS
    REFUSE "the series has no reading for a month between its first and its last (the generator proves it has none missing)"

GIVEN `the rest` IS A LIST OF `A published reading`
      `the month` IS A `A calendar month`
GIVETH A `A published reading`
`the first reading among` `the rest` `that is of` `the month` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the rest`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN `the series has no reading for a month between its first and last`
    WHEN x FOLLOWED BY xs THEN
        IF   x's `the year the reading is of` EQUALS (`the month`'s `year of the month`)
         AND x's `the month the reading is of` EQUALS (`the month`'s `number of the month in the year`)
        THEN x
        ELSE `the first reading among` xs `that is of` `the month`

-- "the index the Bureau publishes" for a month: the reading of that month.
-- src:179 | ”מדד“ – מדד המחירים לצרכן שמפרסמת הלשכה המרכזית לסטטיסטיקה;
@ref ITO s 1 "מדד"; NII s 1 "מדד"; cpi-il35-published-figures.l4
GIVEN `the month` IS A `A calendar month`
GIVETH A `A published reading`
`the reading the Bureau published for` `the month` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the running number of` `the month` LESS THAN `the running number of` `the first month of the published series`
            THEN `the published series begins with January 2000, so the reading this needs is not in it`
        IF `the running number of` `the month` GREATER THAN `the running number of` `the last month of the published series`
            THEN `the published series ends with August 2026, so the reading this needs is not in it`
        OTHERWISE `the first reading among` `the readings the Central Bureau of Statistics published, January 2000 to August 2026` `that is of` `the month`

§ `The index published last before a day`

-- src:180 | ”שיעור עליית המדד“, בתקופה פלונית – ההפרש בין המדד שפורסם לאחרונה לפני סוף התקופה לבין המדד שפורסם לאחרונה לפני תחילת התקופה, מחולק במדד שפורסם לאחרונה לפני תחילת התקופה;
-- Before the START of a month (its first day): a reading published in an earlier month, and the latest of them.
@ref ITO s 1 "שיעור עליית המדד" (source line 180); assumption A1
GIVEN `the month` IS A `A calendar month`
GIVETH A `A published reading`
`the reading last published before the start of` `the month` MEANS
    `the reading the Bureau published for`
        (`the calendar month with running number`
            (`the running number of` `the month` MINUS `the number of months from the month a reading is of to the month it is published in` MINUS 1))

-- Before the END of a month (its last day): readings published in that month itself count.
@ref ITO s 1 "שיעור עליית המדד" (source line 180); assumption A1
GIVEN `the month` IS A `A calendar month`
GIVETH A `A published reading`
`the reading last published before the end of` `the month` MEANS
    `the reading the Bureau published for`
        (`the calendar month with running number`
            (`the running number of` `the month` MINUS `the number of months from the month a reading is of to the month it is published in`))

§ `Restating a reading in an older base`

-- The product of the Bureau's step factors for the bases from `lo` (inclusive) up to `hi` (exclusive).
GIVEN `the bases` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
      `lo`        IS A NUMBER
      `hi`        IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the product of the step factors for` `the bases` `from` `lo` `up to below` `hi` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the bases`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN 1
    WHEN b FOLLOWED BY bs THEN
        (IF b AT LEAST `lo` AND b LESS THAN `hi`
         THEN (CONSIDER `the step factor into base` b
               WHEN JUST f  THEN f
               WHEN NOTHING THEN 1)
         ELSE 1)
        TIMES `the product of the step factors for` bs `from` `lo` `up to below` `hi`

-- A reading restated in an OLDER base (or its own): its value times the step factors of the bases it passes.
-- Restating into a newer base is not needed by anything here and is not offered.
@ref cpi-il35-published-figures.l4: the Bureau's linkage coefficients [cbs-cpi-coef]
GIVEN `the reading` IS A `A published reading`
      `the base year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the value of` `the reading` `restated in base` `the base year` MEANS
    IF   `the base year` GREATER THAN (`the reading`'s `the base year of the reading`)
    THEN `a reading is restated only into its own base or an older one`
    ELSE (`the reading`'s `the value of the reading`)
            TIMES `the product of the step factors for` `the base years of the published series, oldest first`
                    `from` `the base year` `up to below` (`the reading`'s `the base year of the reading`)

@ref cpi-il35-published-figures.l4
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`a reading is restated only into its own base or an older one` MEANS
    REFUSE "a reading is restated only into its own base or an older one; restating into a newer base is not offered"

§ `The rate of rise of the index between two readings`

-- (fork F1) s 1 divides a difference of two readings by the earlier. Where the two are in one base the arithmetic is
-- the Law's own. Where a base changed between them the text does not say how they are compared. Three readings, kept by
-- name (nouns, `A reading of how readings of two bases are compared`): link them through the Bureau's coefficients
-- (restate both in the older base, then s 1's arithmetic); take, for a span of exactly twelve months, the percentage the
-- Bureau published for the twelve months (a rounded figure); or decline. RULED by Meng on 2026-10-08 (SHRUG): declined by
-- default, and answered only where linking and the Bureau's percentage give the same rise (they do not, at the one pair
-- the capstone needs: NOTES.md, fork F1). Within one base there is one reading and it answers.
@ref fork F1; Meng's ruling of 2026-10-08 (SHRUG)
GIVETH A `A reading of how readings of two bases are compared`
`section 1 — the reading this row takes where readings are of two bases` MEANS
    `a rise across a change of base is declined`

@ref fork F1
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the text does not say how readings of two bases are compared, and the two ways open give different answers here` MEANS
    REFUSE "the text does not say how readings of two bases are compared, and the two ways open (linking through the Bureau's coefficients; the percentage the Bureau published for twelve months) give different answers here"

@ref fork F1
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the Bureau's percentage for twelve months covers only a span of exactly twelve months between the same calendar months` MEANS
    REFUSE "the Bureau's percentage for twelve months covers only a span of exactly twelve months between the same calendar months of consecutive years"

-- s 1's arithmetic once both are on one scale.
-- src:180 | ”שיעור עליית המדד“, בתקופה פלונית – ההפרש בין המדד שפורסם לאחרונה לפני סוף התקופה לבין המדד שפורסם לאחרונה לפני תחילת התקופה, מחולק במדד שפורסם לאחרונה לפני תחילת התקופה;
@ref ITO s 1 "שיעור עליית המדד" (source line 180)
GIVEN `the earlier reading` IS A NUMBER
      `the later reading`   IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the rate of rise from` `the earlier reading` `to` `the later reading` MEANS
    (`the later reading` MINUS `the earlier reading`) DIVIDED BY `the earlier reading`

-- The older of two readings' bases.
GIVEN `the one` IS A `A published reading`
      `the other` IS A `A published reading`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the older base of` `the one` `and` `the other` MEANS
    IF (`the one`'s `the base year of the reading`) LESS THAN (`the other`'s `the base year of the reading`)
    THEN (`the one`'s `the base year of the reading`)
    ELSE (`the other`'s `the base year of the reading`)

-- Both readings on one scale, the older base's. (The later reading is the one published last before the END of the period.)
@ref cpi-il35-published-figures.l4: the Bureau's linkage coefficients
GIVEN `the reading published last before the start` IS A `A published reading`
      `the reading published last before the end`   IS A `A published reading`
GIVETH AN `Index readings on one scale for a period`
`the pair linked through the Bureau's coefficients, from` `the reading published last before the start` `to` `the reading published last before the end` MEANS
    `Index readings on one scale for a period`
        WITH `index last published before the start of the period` IS `the value of` `the reading published last before the start` `restated in base` `the older base`
        ,    `index last published before the end of the period`   IS `the value of` `the reading published last before the end` `restated in base` `the older base`
    WHERE
        `the older base` MEANS `the older base of` `the reading published last before the start` `and` `the reading published last before the end`

-- Whether the two readings are of the same calendar month of consecutive years: the only span the Bureau's twelve-month percentage speaks to.
@ref cpi-il35-published-figures.l4: percentYear [cbs-cpi]
GIVEN `the reading published last before the start` IS A `A published reading`
      `the reading published last before the end`   IS A `A published reading`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the two readings are of the same month of consecutive years, from` `the reading published last before the start` `to` `the reading published last before the end` MEANS
        (`the reading published last before the end`'s `the year the reading is of`)
            EQUALS (`the reading published last before the start`'s `the year the reading is of`) PLUS 1
    AND (`the reading published last before the end`'s `the month the reading is of`)
            EQUALS (`the reading published last before the start`'s `the month the reading is of`)

-- The rise the Bureau's twelve-month percentage gives, where it speaks to this span at all.
@ref cpi-il35-published-figures.l4: percentYear [cbs-cpi]
GIVEN `the reading published last before the start` IS A `A published reading`
      `the reading published last before the end`   IS A `A published reading`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the rise the Bureau's twelve-month percentage gives from` `the reading published last before the start` `to` `the reading published last before the end` MEANS
    IF `the two readings are of the same month of consecutive years, from` `the reading published last before the start` `to` `the reading published last before the end`
    THEN (`the reading published last before the end`'s `the percent the Bureau published for the twelve months`) DIVIDED BY 100
    ELSE `the Bureau's percentage for twelve months covers only a span of exactly twelve months between the same calendar months`

-- The rate of rise from the reading published last before the start to the one published last before the end, a fall
-- being a negative rate (the earlier rows treat a fall as a switch of their own; this rule returns the signed rise).
@ref ITO s 1 "שיעור עליית המדד" (source line 180); fork F1
GIVEN `the reading published last before the start` IS A `A published reading`
      `the reading published last before the end`   IS A `A published reading`
      how                                           IS A `A reading of how readings of two bases are compared`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the rate of rise of the index from` `the reading published last before the start` `to` `the reading published last before the end` `, comparing readings of two bases as` how MEANS
    IF   (`the reading published last before the start`'s `the base year of the reading`)
            EQUALS (`the reading published last before the end`'s `the base year of the reading`)
    THEN `the rate of rise from` (`the reading published last before the start`'s `the value of the reading`) `to` (`the reading published last before the end`'s `the value of the reading`)
    ELSE CONSIDER how
         WHEN `readings of two bases are compared by linking them through the Bureau's coefficients` THEN `the linked rate`
         WHEN `a rise over twelve months is the percent the Bureau published for the twelve months` THEN `the percentage rate`
         WHEN `a rise across a change of base is declined` THEN
              IF `the two readings are of the same month of consecutive years, from` `the reading published last before the start` `to` `the reading published last before the end`
                 AND `the linked rate` EQUALS `the percentage rate`
              THEN `the linked rate`
              ELSE `the text does not say how readings of two bases are compared, and the two ways open give different answers here`
    WHERE
        `the linked pair` MEANS
            `the pair linked through the Bureau's coefficients, from` `the reading published last before the start` `to` `the reading published last before the end`
        `the linked rate` MEANS
            `the rate of rise from` (`the linked pair`'s `index last published before the start of the period`)
                `to` (`the linked pair`'s `index last published before the end of the period`)
        `the percentage rate` MEANS
            `the rise the Bureau's twelve-month percentage gives from` `the reading published last before the start` `to` `the reading published last before the end`

-- The same, at the reading the switch names.
@ref ITO s 1 "שיעור עליית המדד" (source line 180); fork F1
GIVEN `the reading published last before the start` IS A `A published reading`
      `the reading published last before the end`   IS A `A published reading`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the rate of rise of the index from` `the reading published last before the start` `to` `the reading published last before the end` MEANS
    `the rate of rise of the index from` `the reading published last before the start` `to` `the reading published last before the end`
        `, comparing readings of two bases as` `section 1 — the reading this row takes where readings are of two bases`

§ `A period, and the readings its rise is taken from`

@ref ITO s 1 "שיעור עליית המדד" (source line 180)
GIVEN `the period` IS A `A period of whole months`
GIVETH A `A published reading`
`the reading last published before the start of the period` `the period` MEANS
    `the reading last published before the start of` (`the period`'s `the first month of the period`)

@ref ITO s 1 "שיעור עליית המדד" (source line 180)
GIVEN `the period` IS A `A period of whole months`
GIVETH A `A published reading`
`the reading last published before the end of the period` `the period` MEANS
    `the reading last published before the end of` (`the period`'s `the last month of the period`)

-- src:180 | ”שיעור עליית המדד“, בתקופה פלונית – ההפרש בין המדד שפורסם לאחרונה לפני סוף התקופה לבין המדד שפורסם לאחרונה לפני תחילת התקופה, מחולק במדד שפורסם לאחרונה לפני תחילת התקופה;
@ref ITO s 1 "שיעור עליית המדד" (source line 180); fork F1
GIVEN `the period` IS A `A period of whole months`
      how          IS A `A reading of how readings of two bases are compared`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the rate of rise of the index in` `the period` `, comparing readings of two bases as` how MEANS
    `the rate of rise of the index from` (`the reading last published before the start of the period` `the period`)
        `to` (`the reading last published before the end of the period` `the period`)
        `, comparing readings of two bases as` how

@ref ITO s 1 "שיעור עליית המדד" (source line 180); fork F1
GIVEN `the period` IS A `A period of whole months`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the rate of rise of the index in` `the period` MEANS
    `the rate of rise of the index in` `the period` `, comparing readings of two bases as` `section 1 — the reading this row takes where readings are of two bases`

-- A period of twelve months beginning with the first day of a month: from the start of that month to the end of the month eleven months on.
-- (A tax year is the one that begins in January.)
@ref ITO s 1 "שנת מס" (source line 202), "שיעור עליית המדד" (source line 180)
GIVEN `the first month` IS A `A calendar month`
GIVETH A `A period of whole months`
`the period of twelve months beginning with` `the first month` MEANS
    `A period of whole months`
        WITH `the first month of the period` IS `the first month`
        ,    `the last month of the period`  IS `the calendar month with running number` (`the running number of` `the first month` PLUS 11)

-- The pair of readings, on one scale, that row IL-03's `Index readings for a period` (and row IL-04's two figures) take as INPUTS.
-- Where the two are of one base they are the Bureau's own figures. Across a change of base they are restated in the older
-- base by linking, answered only where the reading of fork F1 answers the rise at all (declined by default, as the rise is).
@ref ITO s 1 "שיעור עליית המדד" (source line 180); fork F1
GIVEN `the period` IS A `A period of whole months`
      how          IS A `A reading of how readings of two bases are compared`
GIVETH AN `Index readings on one scale for a period`
`the readings on one scale for` `the period` `, comparing readings of two bases as` how MEANS
    IF   (`the first`'s `the base year of the reading`) EQUALS (`the last`'s `the base year of the reading`)
    THEN `Index readings on one scale for a period`
             WITH `index last published before the start of the period` IS (`the first`'s `the value of the reading`)
             ,    `index last published before the end of the period`   IS (`the last`'s `the value of the reading`)
    ELSE CONSIDER how
         WHEN `a rise over twelve months is the percent the Bureau published for the twelve months` THEN
              REFUSE "the Bureau's percentage is a rate, not a pair of readings; ask for the rise, not the pair"
         WHEN `readings of two bases are compared by linking them through the Bureau's coefficients` THEN `the linked pair`
         WHEN `a rise across a change of base is declined` THEN
              IF `the rate of rise of the index in` `the period` `, comparing readings of two bases as` how EQUALS `the rate of the linked pair`
              THEN `the linked pair`
              ELSE `the text does not say how readings of two bases are compared, and the two ways open give different answers here`
    WHERE
        `the first` MEANS `the reading last published before the start of the period` `the period`
        `the last`  MEANS `the reading last published before the end of the period` `the period`
        `the linked pair` MEANS `the pair linked through the Bureau's coefficients, from` `the first` `to` `the last`
        `the rate of the linked pair` MEANS
            `the rate of rise from` (`the linked pair`'s `index last published before the start of the period`) `to` (`the linked pair`'s `index last published before the end of the period`)

@ref ITO s 1 "שיעור עליית המדד" (source line 180); fork F1
GIVEN `the period` IS A `A period of whole months`
GIVETH AN `Index readings on one scale for a period`
`the readings on one scale for` `the period` MEANS
    `the readings on one scale for` `the period` `, comparing readings of two bases as` `section 1 — the reading this row takes where readings are of two bases`
